# A tone from nothing: a one-transistor phase-shift oscillator playing through a speaker.
#
# Q1 is an amplifier like `amplifier`'s, but its input is its own output fed back through three
# capacitor–resistor sections, along the bottom. Each section turns a sine by up to 90°, and at one
# frequency the three together turn it by 180°, which Q1 turns by another 180°: the signal comes back
# to the base the way it left, and if Q1 gains more than the sections lose, a ripple at that frequency
# grows each time round. Three equal sections of 10 kΩ and 10 nF would ring at 1 / (2π · 10k · 10n ·
# √6), about 650 Hz; the third section's resistor here is the base's divider and Q1's own input
# together, nearer 6 kΩ, which brings it down to about 530 Hz.
#
# Nothing starts it but switching it on: the jolt as the capacitors charge has a little of every
# frequency in it, and the loop picks out its own and grows it until Q1 runs out of room to swing,
# which is what holds it there — and why it sounds a little buzzy rather than a pure sine.
#
# Q2 is an emitter follower, buffering the oscillator from the speaker's 8 Ω; CS keeps its DC out of
# the speaker. The speaker plays while the clock runs at a second a second, and `m` mutes it. Press
# `r` to hear it start again from nothing.

speed 1

battery   B1    30 0  30 14  9V
wire            6 0   30 0
wire            4 14  30 14
ground          4 14

# Q1 and its bias.
resistor  RB1   6 0   6 7    100k
resistor  RB2   6 7   6 14   22k
wire            6 7   10 7
resistor  RC    12 0  12 4   4.7k
npn       Q1    12 4  10 7   12 9   2N3904
resistor  RE    12 9  12 14  1k
wire            12 9  9 9
capacitor CE    9 9   9 14   100u

# The phase-shift network, from the collector round underneath to the base.
wire            12 4  14 4
wire            14 4  14 16
capacitor C1    14 16 11 16  10n
resistor  RA    11 16 11 14  10k
capacitor C2    11 16 8 16   10n
resistor  RB    8 16  8 14   10k
capacitor C3    8 16  5 16   10n
wire            5 16  3 16
wire            3 16  3 7
wire            3 7   6 7

# The follower and the speaker.
wire            14 4  18 4
wire            20 0  20 1
npn       Q2    20 1  18 4  20 7   2N3904
resistor  RF    20 7  20 14  220
wire            20 7  23 7
capacitor CS    23 7  26 7   220u
speaker   SPK   26 7  26 14  8

label     osc   14 4
meter     OSC   12 4  12 14
meter     OUT   26 7  26 14
